    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d367">

                <pb facs="0370" n="[346]" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg346"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Haldeman.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 35.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 2, 1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi>Your despatch of December 3, No. 39, has
                    been received. We observe, not without interest, the progress of the controversy
                    concerning the duchy of Holstein, which is now engaging so deeply the attention
                    of the European cabinets. You will, therefore, accept my sincere thanks for the
                    information you have given me on that subject.</p>
                <p>I have laid before the Secretary of the Navy so much of your despatch as relates
                    to the suspected sale of a steamer in Sweden or Denmark. I have also directed
                    the attention of our minister at London to the consul’s statement, that the
                    steamer is expected to be prepared in some British harbor, with a view to run
                    the blockade in some of our southern ports.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jacob S. Haldeman</hi>, Esq., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.,
                            &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stockholm.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
